<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:54Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Serbian student movement eyes power after election triumph</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9066362ac2b63b8774aef2ed9a2e7e614f24337934cfb97ccfccd00e3272da62</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:06:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T19:48:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/serbian-student-movement-eyes-power-after-election-triumph--396143e74db4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/serbian-student-movement-eyes-power-after-election-triumph" /><summary type="html">Emotions ran high in Belgrade on Monday after a student-led movement upset the right-wing populist Aleksandar Vucic's party in Serbia's snap election. A celebratory mood gripped the capital, with drivers honking their horns and passers-by holding up three fingers -- the winning list's ballot number and a Serbian greeting. Many wore badges and other symbols of the student movement, while a large group of residents spent the day cleaning up a park between parliament and the presidency after Vucic loyalists, who had camped there for more than a year, fled. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with researchers and political activist Aleksandar Matković.</summary></entry><entry><title>Comeback kid: How did Brazil veteran-leader Lula upset Bolsonaro?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b16fc5f02763f6614a386104e912f03da865eb2863d4ebe9d3279d6bf3124f2</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T19:22:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261026-comeback-kid-how-did-brazil-veteran-leader-lula-upset-bolsonaro--c3955199ecd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261026-comeback-kid-how-did-brazil-veteran-leader-lula-upset-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Two days shy of his 81st birthday… Brazil’s Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva emerging as the comeback kid. Coming from behind in the polls after a bitter campaign where he often showed his age, Lula becoming the first candidate since Brazil’s return to democracy in the 1980s to win the presidential runoff after trailing in the first round. How did the Workers Party leader turn a 2-point-2 million vote deficit against the far-right's Flavio Bolsonaro into a 4-point-4 million vote win? Reminder that three short weeks ago, most races at the federal and state level broke the way of conservatives and the far-right?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>UN cites 'ethnic cleansing' concerns around Israel's Palestinian displacement operation in Hebron</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8926073d072a76020969ce2386ae072e730fd47aff1bb2264fe054a13679f23c</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:59:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-un-cites-ethnic-cleansing-concerns-around-israel-palestinian-displacement-operation-hebron--f54dc7b36717.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-un-cites-ethnic-cleansing-concerns-around-israel-palestinian-displacement-operation-hebron" /><summary type="html">The United Nations on Monday raised "ethnic cleansing" concerns following Israel's operation to displace by force more than 3,000 Palestinians from their homes in Hebron in the West Bank after two Palestinian gunmen killed two Israeli soldiers at a checkpoint near the city on Friday. UN rights chief Volker Turk said in a statement that the "aggressive operation" must end, and that "collective punishment is a grave violation of international law".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>French student union leaders call for 'continued mobilisation' after meeting PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0fb53de88269c701460939d8449546e91efacfb6ab308dc796ed63fbe9c6912</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:06:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:37:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-french-student-union-leaders-call-for-continued-mobilisation-after-meeting-pm--c60adecb5ed9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-french-student-union-leaders-call-for-continued-mobilisation-after-meeting-pm" /><summary type="html">The French government met student representatives on Monday (October 26) following weeks of unrest. Students who had been demanding a meeting for weeks hail progress. Nonetheless they are now calling for fresh demonstrations next Saturday (October 31) to press for further measures. Details by FRANCE 24’s French Politics Editor Marc Perelman.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil: What does Lula's re-election mean for the Amazon?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7e0874ab476ac6b76ae904917c69618f793eed93a91522c2015f8b5359b0c2b</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:18:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-what-does-lula-s-re-election-mean-for-the-amazon--6f4fc14c1029.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-what-does-lula-s-re-election-mean-for-the-amazon" /><summary type="html">Climate activists in Brazil are celebrating President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's election victory as good news for the Amazon rainforest. His last four years in power saw a record decrease in deforestation in the world's largest rainforest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Opponents accuse Netanyahu of stoking tensions with Iran before Israel's election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:caa04d649c46961eadfb64f1e345f13682d6553a54da3f12a685d6ba3326f336</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:11:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/opponents-accuse-netanyahu-of-stoking-tensions-with-iran-before-israel-s-election--5429441497ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/opponents-accuse-netanyahu-of-stoking-tensions-with-iran-before-israel-s-election" /><summary type="html">Israel's defence minister denied on Monday (October 26) reports of a rift between PM Netanyahu and the army over Iran, before the vote.  Netanyahu has campaigned heavily on his security credentials, insisting only he can "finish the job" in the US-Israeli war on Iran. His main rival, ex-army chief Gadi Eisenkot, has accused him of playing up the Iran threat when it suits him politically, and of failing to accomplish his war goals. FRANCE 24's Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Leaders across Americas react to Brazil President Lula's re-election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:70782ff0e2a4c802493cfef51f38647552cc41933afda2fea3597824fb302900</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:05:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/leaders-across-americas-react-to-brazil-president-lula-s-re-election--efc0688d3f0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/leaders-across-americas-react-to-brazil-president-lula-s-re-election" /><summary type="html">​President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won Brazil's presidential election on Sunday (October 25), defeating right-wing ​Senator Flavio Bolsonaro in a runoff to secure a fourth non-consecutive term.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli candidate Eisenkot pledges to unite country as Netanyahu deems him 'soft' on Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5379cf9d26cf1a130a5086d0fbb9b6725b512dc224491208eef87b5079f049b1</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:58:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-israeli-candidate-eisenkot-pledges-to-unite-israelis-as-netanyahu-deems-him-soft-on-iran--bd8634a89185.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-israeli-candidate-eisenkot-pledges-to-unite-israelis-as-netanyahu-deems-him-soft-on-iran" /><summary type="html">Israeli presidential candidate Gadi Eisenkot's pledge made Sunday to "heal" Israeli society after Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's divisive tenure resonated with some voters attending his final campaign rally before polling begins Tuesday. Netanyahu meanwhile received fresh backing for re-election from US President Donald Trump and deemed Eisenkot "soft" on Iran.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'Lula accustomed to negotiating tough bargains': Campaign promises collide with right-wing Congress</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aec37b397da1d0b97af927392fd9932f046fd32879e262712c1c9c3a65f35361</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:54:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lula-accustomed-to-negotiating-tough-bargains-campaign-promises-collide-with-right-wing-congress--662d1f784eef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lula-accustomed-to-negotiating-tough-bargains-campaign-promises-collide-with-right-wing-congress" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Christopher Sabatini, Director of Chatham House's Latin America Programme. Sabatini examines how Lula's campaign reinvention, youth mobilisation, and the changing dynamics of Bolsonarismo are reshaping Brazil's political landscape. By embracing social media, mobilising younger voters, and shifting attention from his historical achievements to the economic anxieties of ordinary Brazilians, Lula managed to transform the electoral contest. As Sabatini explains, voters were no longer satisfied with hearing about the past. They wanted an answer to a more immediate question: "What are you going to do for us now?</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel election: unable to vote from abroad, expats have to fly home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9a581091813ca92dfd653490de3594abe24db8330fe83cb035b1e4cde830661</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:47:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-election-unable-to-vote-from-abroad-expats-have-to-fly-home--cdb70f36234d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-election-unable-to-vote-from-abroad-expats-have-to-fly-home" /><summary type="html">Israelis can’t vote from abroad, so tens of thousands of expats are expected to fly home for the election. At Tel Aviv airport, supporters of opposition figure Gadi Eisenkot are already waiting at arrivals. A “Fly and Vote” initiative helps expats organise their trip, despite a failed petition from Netanyahu’s Likud party to restrict it. With polls predicting a tight race, every vote could count, and the result will decide the Prime Minister’s fate.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macklemore holds charity stadium shows to raise funds for Palestine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8ae061cbffe5217eee434bfd5933ef96b425f680ca0edf258ef9077bee2c0f8</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:26:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261026-macklemore-holds-charity-stadium-shows-to-raise-funds-for-palestine--cd369e23887b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261026-macklemore-holds-charity-stadium-shows-to-raise-funds-for-palestine" /><summary type="html">In this arts24 music show, Jennifer Ben Brahim brings us a roundup of the big music releases and news of the week, from US rapper Macklemore's charity stadium shows to raise money for Palestine, to the return of R'n'B crooner John Legend with his 11th album "Muse" – his first collaboration with close friend Pharrell Williams.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>France protests: Macron rules out state of emergency – for now</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3120878f93258fab2cf5705e3c0bb32b73144ed02f450e8af2822257fae6915</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:16:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-france-protests-macron-rules-out-state-of-emergency-_-for-now--d78e2f54223a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-france-protests-macron-rules-out-state-of-emergency-%E2%80%93-for-now" /><summary type="html">The French government sought to draw a line Monday under weeks of protests that have been marred by violence, with President Emmanuel Macron heading to Marseille. France has been rocked by widespread anger over the rising cost of living, with nationwide demonstrations on October 17 degenerating into some of the country's worst rioting in years.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula's re-election brings hope for the Amazon as deforestation drops to record low</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40c384b6066c6217b5a4a5b166516e4470a0d77ee6c212d9b3078cfbae534d52</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:12:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261026-lula-s-re-election-brings-hope-for-the-amazon-as-deforestation-drops-to-record-low--5efd7aaf7e54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261026-lula-s-re-election-brings-hope-for-the-amazon-as-deforestation-drops-to-record-low" /><summary type="html">Climate activists in Brazil and beyond are celebrating President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's election victory as good news for the Amazon rainforest. His last four years in power saw a record decrease in deforestation in the world's largest rainforest, appropriately nicknamed the planet's lungs. FRANCE 24's Environment Editor Valerie Dekimpe tells us more.</summary><category term="Down to Earth" /></entry><entry><title>Jordan arrests three after deadly church terror attack, retaliates with strikes on Syria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4088f28bcbc8c3d572db6c490a51046edb000367fff57cea6472ae0055885eb6</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T15:12:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-jordan-arrests-three-following-deadly-terror-attack-on-church--ff7fe6210ee5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-jordan-arrests-three-following-deadly-terror-attack-on-church" /><summary type="html">Jordanian authorities on Monday arrested three suspects over last week's deadly attack that killed nine people in a church funeral procession in the village of Hammoud. Jordan's military later launched strikes on "terrorist organisations" in neighbouring Syria in retaliation for the attack by alleged Islamic extremists.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula reelected president in runoff vote: A look back at his career</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ef6fd966b97944b90d38223218088cfbd3f8c2981e1498b964c9bc519e7d8b9</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T15:11:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-lula-reelected-president-in-runoff-vote-a-look-back-at-his-career--7ab7020c363f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-lula-reelected-president-in-runoff-vote-a-look-back-at-his-career" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won an unprecedented fourth term on Sunday (October 25), the country's electoral court said, in a shock result that defied polls.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms 2026: A history of gerrymandering</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:592df132255233f209feaa6b490f46aeb250c98207303ec58c74108f19c6ab23</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:48:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-2026-a-history-of-gerrymandering--2a4bc0975c37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-2026-a-history-of-gerrymandering" /><summary type="html">What does a salamander have to do with US elections? Dating back centuries, gerrymandering continues to play a role in American elections today. Used more often by Republicans in the modern era of voting, Democrats have also resorted to the tactic in the past decade. But what is gerrymandering, and why is it called that? FRANCE 24's Tanishk Saha explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron promises 'concrete measures' in response to French students' demands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5348280ea58e7db7fd37518a3db010d02a9c494bd8331a90e5f4a88507322b44</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:05:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:39:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-french-president-promises-concrete-measures-in-response-to-french-students-demands" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron said the government would announce “concrete measures" on Monday (October 26) to address school students’ demands after weeks of unrest. Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu was scheduled to meet with students later Monday. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Obama blasts Trump's 'chaos and cruelty' while campaigning for Democrats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6969ae6e0d2dbe1139e3f5aa9fa726d4111fcbe517c66d02334af789965e0150</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:28:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-obama-blasts-trump-s-chaos-and-cruelty-while-campaigning-for-democrats--abf7926435d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-obama-blasts-trump-s-chaos-and-cruelty-while-campaigning-for-democrats" /><summary type="html">Ten days out from the elections that will determine control of the closely divided Congress, Barack Obama took to the campaign trail to accuse the Republican president of corruption, deride his strategy for Iran and skewer the gilded aesthetic he has applied ‌to White House renovations. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands of Israelis living abroad expected to fly in for pivotal vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d960a0b9f8c15be62df1f40ff3f4c57885fa935acad020af5bec431a3e0c197c</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:20:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-of-israelis-living-abroad-expected-to-fly-in-for-pivotal-vote--a3d6b8696ede.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-of-israelis-living-abroad-expected-to-fly-in-for-pivotal-vote" /><summary type="html">Israelis are preparing to head to the polls on Tuesday (October 27). Unable to vote from abroad, tens of thousands of expatriate citizens have been flying in from across the world to cast their ballots. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky met some of them at the airport.</summary></entry><entry><title>Serbia's Vucic concedes defeat to the student-led movement: What's next?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e3be2dc575ceb596a36f3d42665c893b00bde8b4a624430976e1e315ae6e702</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:12:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/serbia-s-vucic-concedes-defeat-to-the-student-led-movement-what-s-next--ca4d04c9c348.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/serbia-s-vucic-concedes-defeat-to-the-student-led-movement-what-s-next" /><summary type="html">Serbia's student-led protest movement won a historic victory in parliamentary ⁠election, ending the ​long rule of Aleksandar Vucic and sparking mass celebrations. But their yet-to-be named leaders face a long list of issues. FRANCE 24's Angela Diffley gives us her analysis.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula wins fourth term: What are the reactions in Brazil?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24983c18f5431754979991592f0150e978b29294896684dede0fc35871a49d13</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:04:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lula-wins-fourth-term-what-are-the-reactions-in-brazil--6fac97bd28ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lula-wins-fourth-term-what-are-the-reactions-in-brazil" /><summary type="html">Brazil's leftist President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva was re-elected against all expectations on Sunday (October 25), but his conservative rival Flavio Bolsonaro refused to accept the loss and said he would seek to have the vote annulled. FRANCE 24's Jan Onoszko tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bolsonaro's refusal to concede underscores ‘serious’ challenges to Brazil's democratic institutions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:201f7ccee4572a34701e877c70cc14413962e05f652ff05c16259a851fb3002b</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:53:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-s-refusal-to-concede-underscores-serious-challenges-to-brazil-s-democratic-institutions--61d6451f7b79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-s-refusal-to-concede-underscores-serious-challenges-to-brazil-s-democratic-institutions" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome Dr Pedro Perfeito da Silva, Latin American specialist at the University of Exeter. For Dr Perfeito da Silva, Lula's stunning success reflects the convergence of digital organizing, grassroots mobilization, targeted socioeconomic appeals and an effective effort to mobilise opposition to the Bolsonaro political project. As he explains, Lula assembled a coalition that "not only energized his supporters but also attracted voters from groups that had been somewhat skeptical of the government in the first round."</summary></entry><entry><title>Will Netanyahu's security promise win him this election?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26227a64a0f2c5de147150d687026283f38ac7a2a08ca56283fe065d3c967ec5</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:07:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:52:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-will-netanyahu-s-security-promise-win-him-this-election--7245e677289a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-will-netanyahu-s-security-promise-win-him-this-election" /><summary type="html">Since the beginning of his political career, Benjamin Netanyahu, Israel's longest-serving prime minister, has campaigned on a promise that he is the only one who will keep the Jewish state safe. As Israelis head to the polls for their first election since the October7 Hamas attacks and the start of the war in Gaza, Netanyahu's strategy might be less effective. FRANCE 24's Gabrielle Nadler explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula wins Brazil election but faces uphill battle to govern</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd000ce81ec66d6362c1205dc82824f506bd720a0a2ebd30eb6a8f69e25f6db9</id><updated>2026-10-26T21:05:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:38:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-lula-wins-brazil-election-but-faces-uphill-battle-to-govern" /><summary type="html">Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's narrow election victory on Sunday has dealt a blow to Brazil's far right, but deep political divisions remain. The newly re-elected president must tackle economic and security concerns at home while navigating international tensions with US President Donald Trump.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
